# CHANGELOG.md: pull requests add changelog.d/ fragments instead of editing it
# (changelog.d/README.md). Before fragments, every PR added its entry at the top
# of "Unreleased", so two PRs in flight always touched the same lines. The union driver keeps both sides'
# added lines instead of reporting a conflict. It also keeps BOTH versions of
# a line two branches each edited, so check the merged changelog when a merge
# touches an existing entry. Applies to local merges and rebases; GitHub's
# own "has conflicts" check and web merges ignore custom merge drivers.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
